  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Course: Learn C++ OOP"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Previously, we learned about the public and private access modifiers in the OOP (Basics) chapter. Let's revise what these access modifiers do:"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "public members - accessible from outside the class",
        "private members - not accessible from outside the class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In this lesson, we'll learn about the protected access modifier."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "C++ Protected Members"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Similar to public and private, we use the protected keyword to declare protected class members in C++. For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "class Person {\n  protected:\n    int id;\n\n  public:\n    string name;\n};"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here,"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "id is protected",
        "name is public"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Once we declare a variable/function protected, it can be only accessed from that class and its derived classes. If we try to access it from somewhere else, we will get an error. For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "1#include <iostream>\n2using namespace std;\n3\n4class Person {\n5\n6    protected:\n7        int id;\n8\n9\n10    public:\n11        string name;\n12};\n13\n14int main() {\n15\n16    // create an object of Person\n17    Person person;\n18    \n19    // access the public variable\n20    person.name = \"Jon Snow\";\n21    cout << \"Name: \" << person.name << endl;\n22    \n23\n24    // error: protected members cannot be accessed\n25    person.id = 101;\n26    cout << \"ID: \" << person.id << endl;\n27\n28\n29    return 0;\n30}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When we run this code, we will get an error:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "ERROR!   22 |     person.id = 101;\n      |            ^~\n    6 |         int id;\n      |             ^~\n   23 |     cout << \"ID: \" << person.id << endl;\n      |                              ^~\n    6 |         int id;\n      |             ^~"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This error arises because we are trying to access the protected variable id from the main() function (outside the Person class)."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Protected members cannot be accessed from outside the class or its subclasses.",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
